   "core/parsers/costco_ecom.py - Costco US .com PO (Wrangler, 9 pages).\n\nThe .com PO (72000167) prints ONE line-item per (colour x label-code) across\npages 1-5 (``1662 BLU BLUE CINT26 ELP 3 19 1,560 $5.34 $8,330.40``) plus a\ncolour x label-code summary grid on page 6. There are no XS..XL sizes on this\nPO — instead pages 7-8 print a \"size-run\" block per label code, each mapping\nthat DM-PK label code to exactly ONE numeric OWA size (``IWO->2 ELO->4 ELP->6\nELQ->8 ELR->10 ELS->12 ELT->14 ELU->16``). The OSR ``Size`` column therefore\ncarries the numeric size, resolved from those blocks; when a code is missing\nfrom the size-run blocks it falls back to the raw label code (no regression).\n\nHeader block is identical to costco_hybrid (same 5 STAR APPAREL template), so\n``_extract_costco_header`` is shared. ISOLATED: only the line-item extraction is\nnew; costco_hybrid / line_items / matrix_* are untouched.\n",
