   "Map each DM-PK label code to its single numeric OWA size.\n\n    Pages 7-8 print one block per label code; each block has exactly one\n    non-zero column in the size sequence:\n\n        ELO\n        OWA 2 4 6 8 10 12 14 16 TTL Units\n        0 1 0 0 0 0 0 0 1        <- size \"4\" is the non-zero column\n        TTL PPK: 1\n\n    ``dimpk_codes`` is the set of label codes seen in the line-items (the only\n    codes we care about). A block may straddle a page boundary (the code line\n    sits at the bottom of page 7 while its ``OWA`` header starts page 8), so we\n    anchor on each code line and scan *forward* a bounded window rather than\n    assuming the header immediately follows it.\n\n    Returns ``{label_code: size_str}``; codes with no resolvable size are\n    omitted so the caller can fall back to the raw code.\n    ",
